                <track-text descriptor="document-title" x="350" y="562" alignment="6" visibility="9" dx="9013" dy="9913" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1984" screen-dy="2828">F-Pn Thibault-IIIn Venetiis 7.7br 1712</track-text>
                <track-text descriptor="document-author" x="992" y="207" alignment="0" visibility="1" dx="9790" dy="5477" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1984" screen-dy="2828"/>
                <track-text descriptor="document-source" x="221" y="1069" alignment="6" visibility="9" dx="3898" dy="18856" cx="0" cy="0" screen-dx="1984" screen-dy="2828">Source: F-Pn RÃ©s Vmc ms. 61Olim: Library of Mad. ThibaultLikely, the frontpage of this manuscript was switchedwith that of ms Vma 1213 (Weiss Ã  Rome).Weiss was in Rome from after 1708 until 1714,while many works in ms 1213 can be dated after 1740.</track-text>
